      "preview": "The First Fissure in the Leviathan The Summary This artifact documents a moment of profound legal optimism during the Age of Institutional Exhaustion. The author celebrates a circuit court ruling, McNutt vs. DOJ, as a principled defense of liberty against federal overreach. He believed the judici...",
      "body": "### The First Fissure in the Leviathan\r\n\r\n\r\n#### The Summary\r\nThis artifact documents a moment of profound legal optimism during the Age of Institutional Exhaustion. The author celebrates a circuit court ruling, *McNutt vs. DOJ*, as a principled defense of liberty against federal overreach. He believed the judiciary was re-establishing the original intent of constitutional powers, specifically limiting the state's ability to use taxation as a regulatory weapon. The analysis posits that this legal precedent would liberate key industries, particularly energy, from the control of a centralized administrative state.\r\n\r\nThrough the Hindsight Filter, we recognize this interpretation as a catastrophic misreading of events. The author saw a system correcting itself; we see a system losing its coherence. The *McNutt* decision was not a sign of a state being rationally constrained by its own laws, but rather a symptom of its own internal dissolution. The legal arguments over the proper use of the Taxing Power versus the Commerce Clause were scholastic debates occurring on the deck of a sinking ship. The author thought he was witnessing a restoration of principle; he was actually documenting an early, formal acknowledgment of the federal government's evaporating authority, a key accelerant of the Great Fragmentation.\r\n\r\n#### The Three-Act Constellation\r### Act I: The Devolution Mandate (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r### Act II: The Sovereignty Contests (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r### Act III: The Rise of the Stacks (Post-2060s)",
