      "preview": "The Measure of the Schism This artifact is a work of bureaucratic polling, presented with the dry neutrality of a non-profit. It is measuring public trust in the federal government. To the authors, the data shows a partisan flip—Republicans trusting the new administration, Democrats losing faith....",
      "body": "# The Measure of the Schism\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of bureaucratic polling, presented with the dry neutrality of a non-profit. It is measuring public trust in the federal government. To the authors, the data shows a partisan flip—Republicans trusting the new administration, Democrats losing faith. They see a \"predictable\" pattern.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this report as the seismograph reading of the final, irreparable fracture of the American political psyche. The \"schism\" described here is not just a difference of opinion; it is a divergence of reality. This document proves that by 2025, the concept of a \"neutral\" federal government had ceased to exist in the minds of the people. It was seen only as a weapon, trusted when held by friends and feared when held by enemies.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of this divergence, from the polling data of your time to the separate realities of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Death of the Neutral State (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Two Governments (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Privatized State (Post-2060s)",
