      "preview": "The Paralysis of the Empty Nest This artifact is a psychometric portrait of a civilization engaging in passive suicide. The Pew Research Center, with its characteristic precision, has captured a profound cognitive dissonance: the American people correctly identified that their society was dying (...",
      "body": "# The Paralysis of the Empty Nest\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a psychometric portrait of a civilization engaging in passive suicide. The Pew Research Center, with its characteristic precision, has captured a profound cognitive dissonance: the American people correctly identified that their society was dying (the negative impact of fewer children), yet they simultaneously refused to empower their government to save it.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this poll not as a policy debate, but as the final proof that the 20th-century nation-state had lost the mandate of heaven. The people did not trust the state with the most fundamental task of any species: its own propagation. They saw the cliff, but they refused to let the driver touch the wheel.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this paralysis, from the \"tax credits\" of your time to the survival mandates of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Vote of No Confidence (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: [[The Great Culling]] of the Secular (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: [[The Sacred Duty]] (Post-2060s)",
