      "preview": "The Academic History of the Great Divergence This artifact is a work of meticulous, dense, and slightly weary historiography. The author, a French historian writing in 2018, is reviewing the recent surge in academic work on eugenics, race science, and biological determinism. He notes a paradox: j...",
      "body": "# The Academic History of the Great Divergence\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of meticulous, dense, and slightly weary historiography. The author, a French historian writing in 2018, is reviewing the recent surge in academic work on eugenics, race science, and biological determinism. He notes a paradox: just as historians were finally deconstructing these concepts, they were roaring back into public and scientific life, fueled by genomics and the Human Genome Project.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a literature review, but as a chronicle of the intellectual skirmishes that preceded the Great Divergence. The author is documenting the moment when the \"blank slate\" consensus of the late 20th century began to crack under the weight of new genetic data. He sees a \"defensive\" posture among social scientists. We see the last, desperate attempt of the old academic order to hold back the tide of the Biotech Faction.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, branching history of the ideas this article reviews, from the \"scandalization\" of the 20th century to the speciation of the 21st.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Return of the Repressed (2000s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Splintering of the Biopolitical (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Reality of the Phyla (Post-2060s)",
