      "preview": "The Eulogy for the Linear Mind This artifact is a work of profound and terrifying sorrow. It is a eulogy delivered by a man standing in the ruins of a library, watching the roof cave in. The author, James Marriott, is not merely a cultural critic; he is a cognitive anthropologist witnessing the e...",
      "body": "# The Eulogy for the Linear Mind\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of profound and terrifying sorrow. It is a eulogy delivered by a man standing in the ruins of a library, watching the roof cave in. The author, James Marriott, is not merely a cultural critic; he is a cognitive anthropologist witnessing the extinction of a species: the Homo lector, the reading man. He correctly identifies that the foundation of the 20th-century world—democracy, science, reason—was built on the specific neurological architecture created by deep reading. And he sees, with devastating clarity, that this architecture is being dismantled by the screen.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a warning, but as the clinical explanation for why [[The Great Fragmentation]] was inevitable. A civilization that loses the capacity for linear thought loses the capacity for linear history. It collapses into the \"narcissistic eternal present\" that the author describes, and from there, into chaos.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of the \"post-literate society,\" from the dying universities of your time to the guarded scriptoriums of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Unraveling of the Civic Mind (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Second Feudalism (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Scriptoriums (Post-2060s)",
