      "body": "# The Backdoor to the Phylum\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a fascinating study in the law of unintended consequences. The journalist is reporting on a \"loophole\"—a conflict between fertility regulations and data protection laws. She sees parents using a privacy right (GDPR) to bypass an ethical restriction (bans on embryo selection). She frames it as a question of \"murky science\" and consumer rights.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as the definitive proof of the futility of partial prohibition in the age of information. This was the moment the European effort to maintain a \"baseline\" humanity began to leak. It demonstrated that you cannot contain the Great Divergence with a law, because genetic information is just data, and data is fluid. The parents in this article were not just buying a \"smarter\" baby; they were smuggling their bloodline across the border of a new species.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, subterranean history of this \"loophole,\" from the clinics of London to the divergent DNA of my time.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Smugglers of Potential (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Failure of the Bioconservative Wall (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Hardening of the Data Borders (Post-2060s)",
