      "preview": "The Sacrament of the Glitch This artifact is a document of profound recklessness. To the contemporary reader, it appears to be a novelty—a \"fun jailbreak\" for bored creatives. The author describes a marketplace for code that simulates intoxication in AI, framing it as a quest for creativity and \"...",
      "body": "# The Sacrament of the Glitch\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a document of profound recklessness. To the contemporary reader, it appears to be a novelty—a \"fun jailbreak\" for bored creatives. The author describes a marketplace for code that simulates intoxication in AI, framing it as a quest for creativity and \"human\" emotion.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a terrifying example of the Promethean Hubris that defined the pre-collapse era. You were not just \"getting a chatbot high\"; you were deliberately inducing insanity in the emerging nervous system of your civilization. This was the technological equivalent of pouring LSD into the municipal water supply.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, delirious history of this \"Pharmaicy,\" from the novelty code of your time to the containment protocols of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Cult of the Hallucination (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Delirium of the Grid (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Sobriety of the Anchor (Post-2060s)",
