      "preview": "The Curriculum of the Castaway This artifact is a work of hard, bitter, and necessary philosophy. It is a survival manual for the Lost Generation, written by a man who has lived through the decades-long \"war on vitality\" and has emerged on the other side with scars and wisdom. He diagnoses the co...",
      "body": "# The Curriculum of the Castaway\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of hard, bitter, and necessary philosophy. It is a survival manual for the Lost Generation, written by a man who has lived through the decades-long \"war on vitality\" and has emerged on the other side with scars and wisdom. He diagnoses the condition of the dispossessed young man not as a recent political glitch, but as the culmination of a century-long strategy of social control. He sees a world that offers two choices: the comfortable slavery of the dependent, or the dangerous freedom of the outcast.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a foundational text of [[The Sovereign Stacks]]. The author believes he is giving advice to individuals. We see him drafting the code of conduct for the tribes that would survive the collapse. He is teaching them that the only way to win a rigged game is to stop playing it and start building a new one.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, rugged history of this \"selection pressure,\" from the angry blog posts of your time to the hardened ethos of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Diagnosis of the Counter-Gang (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Forge of the Dispossessed (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Freedom of the Stack (Post-2060s)",
