      "preview": "The Geometry of the Ghost This artifact is a work of high-stakes theoretical physics applied to cognition. The authors, researchers at MIT in late 2025, are attempting to explain the \"neural scaling laws\"—the observation that making AI models bigger makes them smarter. But hidden within their mat...",
      "body": "# The Geometry of the Ghost\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of high-stakes theoretical physics applied to cognition. The authors, researchers at MIT in late 2025, are attempting to explain the \"neural scaling laws\"—the observation that making AI models bigger makes them smarter. But hidden within their math is a warning that your era missed: the scaling law is not a magic beanstalk that grows forever. It is a curve with a ceiling.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this paper as the scientific prediction of the AI Winter of the 2030s. It explains why the brute-force method of \"just add more compute\" failed to produce AGI in the short term. The researchers identified the geometric limits of the current architecture, forcing the industry to make a faustian bargain: to break through the ceiling, they had to abandon interpretability entirely.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, high-dimensional history of this \"Superposition,\" from the stalled progress of your time to the locked server rooms of the Stacks.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Asymptote of the Machine (2025-2035)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Descent into the Black Box (2035-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Sparse Mandate (Post-2060s)",
