      "preview": "The Manual of the Divorce This artifact is a work of desperate, crystalline logic. The author, a historian staring into the abyss of his own era, has stopped bargaining with reality. He has accepted that the 20th-century rules of engagement—voting, lawsuits, editorials—are dead. He is no longer t...",
      "body": "# The Manual of the Divorce\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of desperate, crystalline logic. The author, a historian staring into the abyss of his own era, has stopped bargaining with reality. He has accepted that the 20th-century rules of engagement—voting, lawsuits, editorials—are dead. He is no longer trying to save the system; he is trying to figure out how to survive its capture.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a blog post, but as the Articles of Secession for the cognitive and managerial elite of the American coasts. The author believes he is proposing radical options to \"force structural changes.\" We see him drafting the operating manual for [[The Great Dissolution]]. He outlined the precise mechanisms—financial decoupling, nullification, and foreign alignment—that would turn the United States from a nation into a memory.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of these \"options,\" from the desperate theories of 2025 to the hardened borders of my time.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Strategy of Soft Secession (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Bifurcation of Capital (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Irony of the Outcome (Post-2060s)",
      "month": "February",
      "glossary_refs": [
        "The Great Dissolution"
      ],
