      "preview": "The Psychology of the Void This artifact is a dispatch from the front lines of the Great De-Accreditation. The author, a therapist with four decades of experience, is documenting the systemic collapse of trust in psychological science. He chronicles the \"replication crisis\" not as an academic deb...",
      "body": "# The Psychology of the Void\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the front lines of the Great De-Accreditation. The author, a therapist with four decades of experience, is documenting the systemic collapse of trust in psychological science. He chronicles the \"replication crisis\" not as an academic debate, but as a betrayal of ordinary people—Marcus in his bathroom, Jennifer at brunch, David making his daughter cry.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for the Crisis of Meaning. The author believes he is exposing bad science. We see him describing the moment when the \"expert class\" lost its ability to define human nature, leaving a vacuum that would be filled by [[The Neotribes]] and the [[Synthetic Deities]].\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"garbage psychology,\" from the TED Talks of your time to the hardened minds of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Collapse of the High Priests (2010s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Psychological Sorting (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Engineering of the Mind (Post-2060s)",
