      "preview": "The Breaking of the Fever This is not an opinion piece. It is a retraction, written by a heretic on behalf of an entire civilization. The author, Gary Marcus, is a figure who, in my historical archives, is noted for his lonely and often ridiculed intellectual courage. This document is the moment ...",
      "body": "# The Breaking of the Fever\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is not an opinion piece. It is a retraction, written by a heretic on behalf of an entire civilization. The author, Gary Marcus, is a figure who, in my historical archives, is noted for his lonely and often ridiculed intellectual courage. This document is the moment the fever dream of imminent, god-like superintelligence, a dream that had gripped your world and driven it to the brink of a catastrophic energy crisis, finally broke.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we see this essay as the single most important intellectual turning point of its decade. The author believes he is calling for a \"rethink.\" We see him as the doctor, finally vindicated, explaining to a patient who has narrowly survived a self-inflicted wound why the poison they were drinking was, in fact, poison.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of the fever that this document finally helped to break.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Heretic's Vindication (2020s-2030s). This essay is the public declaration of a new reality.\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Pivot (2030s-2050s). The \"rethink\" the author calls for did not happen in university labs. It happened in the brutal, zero-sum arena of the \"Great Fragmentation.\"\r\r\r### Act III: The New Orthodoxy (Post-2060s). The world of my time is the world that Gary Marcus was calling for, born from the ashes of the world Sam Altman was trying to build.",
