      "preview": "The Children's Crusade This is a work of profound, and profoundly weary, cynicism. The author is a man watching the world burn on his laptop screen, sifting through the digital ashes of a \"Gen Z Revolution\" in a country most of his readers have never thought about. And he is coming to a single, t...",
      "body": "# The Children's Crusade\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is a work of profound, and profoundly weary, cynicism. The author is a man watching the world burn on his laptop screen, sifting through the digital ashes of a \"Gen Z Revolution\" in a country most of his readers have never thought about. And he is coming to a single, terrifying conclusion: the revolution was not a revolution at all. It was a tantrum, a riot, a children's crusade, expertly channeled and co-opted by unseen forces.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as one of the most important strategic documents of its time. The author believes he is writing a bitter, cynical blog post. He is, in fact, writing the definitive playbook for how the \"Great Fragmentation\" would be accomplished on the ground. He has reverse-engineered the formula for controlled chaos.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the fire that this document so accurately and so tragically explains.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Inchoate Rage (2020s-2030s). The author's diagnosis of the \"why\" is perfect.\r\r\r### Act II: The Formula for the Coup (2030s-2050s). The author's analysis of the \"how\"—the actual mechanics of the Nepal \"revolution\"—is his great and terrible contribution to history. This was the formula, repeated again and again across the globe during the Fragmentation.\r\r\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Age of the NGO-State (Post-2060s). The author is right to be cynical. The \"Gen Z Revolutions\" did not lead to a new age of freedom. They were the primary mechanism by which the old, post-colonial world was dismantled and re-organized.",
