      "preview": "The Quiet Revolutionaries This is a landmark artifact. It is not an article about education. It is the secret history of a quiet, and ultimately world-changing, revolution. The author is chronicling the story of two strange and brilliant heretics who, driven by a shared hatred of \"school,\" accide...",
      "body": "# The Quiet Revolutionaries\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is a landmark artifact. It is not an article about education. It is the secret history of a quiet, and ultimately world-changing, revolution. The author is chronicling the story of two strange and brilliant heretics who, driven by a shared hatred of \"school,\" accidentally invented the future of the human mind.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as one of the most important historical documents of its time. While the great nations and corporations were fighting their loud, stupid wars over the carcass of the 20th century, Joe Liemandt and MacKenzie Price were quietly building the operating system for the 21st. They were not trying to reform the system. They were building its replacement.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, world-altering history of the quiet revolution that began in a garage in Austin, Texas.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Gospel of the Hated School (2020s-2030s). This article is the perfect origin story for the new world.\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Schism in the Nursery (2030s-2050s). The launch of Timeback was not a product launch. It was a declaration of war. It was the spark that ignited the \"Great Schism in the Nursery.\"\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Mind (Post-2060s). The author asks what kind of \"mind virus\" the Timeback of China or Russia might incept. He was more right than he knew. The world of my time is a world of different minds.",
      "month": "October",
