      "preview": "The Council of Ghosts This artifact is a dispatch from the high summer of 20th-century optimism, a gathering of its most capable minds . The World Economic Forum has convened its Global Future Councils, a collection of over 500 leaders from government, business, and civil society, to create \"futu...",
      "body": "# The Council of Ghosts\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the high summer of 20th-century optimism, a gathering of its most capable minds . The World Economic Forum has convened its Global Future Councils, a collection of over 500 leaders from government, business, and civil society, to create \"future-ready solutions\" for the world's most complex problems . They speak of \"dialogue,\" \"collective action,\" and \"global cooperation\" as the keys to a secure and prosperous future .\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this document not as a plan for the future, but as a group portrait of the last, great, sincere generation of a dying order. It is a perfect artifact of the \"Age of Institutional Exhaustion\" . These are the world's pilots, earnestly debating the flight plan, unaware that the engines are on fire and the wings are about to fall off.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, tragic history of the beautiful and irrelevant ideas this council championed.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Illusion of Control (2020s-2030s). This meeting was the high-water mark of the 20th-century elite. They genuinely believed that \"dialogue\" and \"public-private collaboration\" were the tools to manage the 21st century . Their entire framework was built on the assumption of a stable, global, cooperative order. This was their fatal blind spot. They were attempting to apply the tools of institutional consensus-building at the very moment those institutions were losing all legitimacy . They were trying to steer a ship that was already breaking apart in the first swells of the \"Great Fragmentation\" .\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Sovereigns (Post-2060s). The world of my time, the \"Era of Systemic Resilience\" , was not built by a global council of \"thought leaders\" . It was built by the survivors of the collapse, from the bottom up. The problems of the 2020s were not \"solved.\" They were rendered obsolete.",
