      "preview": "The Final, Sane Prescription https://www.vox.com/the-highlight/466025/ai-jobs-chatgpt-agi This is a landmark artifact. It is a work of profound, and profoundly rational, anxiety. The author, a member of the \"laptop class\" he correctly fears is becoming obsolete, is looking at the horizon and seei...",
      "body": "# The Final, Sane Prescription\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://www.vox.com/the-highlight/466025/ai-jobs-chatgpt-agi\r\nThis is a landmark artifact. It is a work of profound, and profoundly rational, anxiety. The author, a member of the \"laptop class\" he correctly fears is becoming obsolete, is looking at the horizon and seeing the approach of a great, automating god. He is performing a clear-eyed and correct diagnosis of the economic apocalypse this god threatens to unleash: a \"neofeudal\" world where the value of human labor collapses to zero, leaving the masses in a state of permanent dependency on a new oligarchy of AI owners.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as the final, sane prescription written for a patient who was already in the terminal stages of a different, and much more acute, disease. The author's fear was correct. His analysis of the economic danger was impeccable. The solutions he gestures toward—strengthening institutions, distributing capital—were the right ones. The tragedy is that he was a brilliant economist diagnosing a coming financial crisis, not realizing the patient's entire physical and institutional structure was already suffering from catastrophic organ failure.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the apocalypse that came—an apocalypse that was not economic, but physical.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Great Displacement (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r### Act II: The Veto of Physics (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Social Contract (Post-2060s)",
