      "preview": "The Gospel of the Spectacle This is an artifact of profound spiritual significance. The author is doing excellent journalism, chronicling a controversy at the intersection of faith and technology. He sees a for-profit company using AI to create \"edutainment,\" and a group of theologians warning th...",
      "body": "# The Gospel of the Spectacle\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is an artifact of profound spiritual significance. The author is doing excellent journalism, chronicling a controversy at the intersection of faith and technology. He sees a for-profit company using AI to create \"edutainment,\" and a group of theologians warning that this cheapens the sacred text, reducing it to a \"Marvel Universe of faith.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we see this not as a business story or a theological debate. We see it as the birth announcement of a new and terrifyingly powerful form of religion. This was not a new way to read the Bible; it was a new way to forge a tribe. The controversy was the last gasp of the old, literate faith, just before the coming of the new, visceral, and all-consuming faith of the spectacle.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, world-altering history of the \"Marvel Universe of faith\" this document heralds.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Cure for the Void (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Forging of the Tribe (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Liturgy (Post-2060s)",
