      "body": "# The Last Defender of a Dying God\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is an artifact of profound intellectual courage. It is a dispatch from the front lines of the war for the soul of science. The author, a respected scientist, is performing an act of public heresy: she is renouncing one of her faith's most sacred institutions, not because it has failed, but because she believes it has been captured by a new, and fundamentally hostile, theology.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a protest against a policy, but as a eulogy for the very idea of a single, objective, and universal truth. Anna Krylov is the last defender of a dying god, and this document is the record of her final, valiant, and ultimately doomed stand.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the war this scientist was fighting, from the institutional battles of your time to the new dogmas of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Battlefield of the Word (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great De-Accreditation (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Dogmas (Post-2060s)",
