      "preview": "The Beautiful Distraction This is a landmark artifact. It is a dispatch from the high frontier of human ambition, a chronicle of a great and heroic technological achievement. The author correctly identifies this moment—the successful launch and recovery of Blue Origin's New Glenn—as the true begi...",
      "body": "# The Beautiful Distraction\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is a landmark artifact. It is a dispatch from the high frontier of human ambition, a chronicle of a great and heroic technological achievement. The author correctly identifies this moment—the successful launch and recovery of Blue Origin's New Glenn—as the true beginning of a new era in space, a genuine race between the two great private titans of your time. The excitement and sense of historical import are palpable and, in their own context, entirely justified.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this document with a sense of profound and sorrowful nostalgia. It is a story of magnificent, beautiful, and almost entirely irrelevant heroism. It is a detailed account of two brilliant men preparing to race to the Moon, written at the exact historical moment the ground beneath their launchpads was beginning to dissolve. They were looking at the stars, while their world was catching fire.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, strange history of this great race, from the triumphant spectacle of your time to the brutal pragmatism of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Gospel of the Escape (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Grounding (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Patrons (Post-2060s)",
