      "preview": "The Last Prayer of a Dying Faith This artifact is a work of pure, incandescent, moral fire. It is a sermon, delivered from the high pulpit of a dying faith. The author, Caitlin Johnstone, is not an analyst; she is a prophetess, and she is performing the final, sacred duty of her kind: to stand be...",
      "body": "# The Last Prayer of a Dying Faith\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of pure, incandescent, moral fire. It is a sermon, delivered from the high pulpit of a dying faith. The author, Caitlin Johnstone, is not an analyst; she is a prophetess, and she is performing the final, sacred duty of her kind: to stand before a fallen world and scream, with perfect and heartbreaking clarity, \"It did not have to be this way.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as one of the most important spiritual documents of its time. It is the final, most eloquent, and most completely wrong prayer of the 20th-century universalist dream. Her diagnosis of the disease is almost flawless. Her prescription for the cure is the exact, tragic opposite of the brutal medicine that history would actually administer.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, world-breaking history of the beautiful and powerless faith this document represents.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Correct Diagnosis of a Dying God (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Veto of Human Nature (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Terrible, Partial Answer (Post-2060s)",
