      "preview": "The Architect of the Fortress This artifact is a work of profound historical importance. It is a dispatch from the engine room of a great and violent reordering of the world. The author, a journalist, is interviewing a man who is not merely a government official, but one of the chief architects o...",
      "body": "# The Architect of the Fortress\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of profound historical importance. It is a dispatch from the engine room of a great and violent reordering of the world. The author, a journalist, is interviewing a man who is not merely a government official, but one of the chief architects of a new global reality. The trade representative, Jamieson Greer, speaks with the calm, pragmatic, and unapologetic confidence of a man who believes he is on the right side of history, dismantling a failed, 70-year-old system and building something stronger in its place.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a political interview, but as a primary source document from the founding of my own world. Greer is not a chaotic actor; he is a brilliant and clear-eyed strategist. And the strategy he so calmly outlines is the very blueprint for [[The Great Fragmentation]]. He believes he is saving the American nation-state. We have the hindsight to know he was, in fact, building the economic foundations for the fortified, competing North American sovereignties that would rise from its grave.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the world this architect was designing.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Gospel of the Physical (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Sorting (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Fortress Americas (Post-2060s)",
