      "preview": "The Autopsy of the Common Good This is a landmark artifact. It is a work of forensic sociology, an autopsy of a dying civic body. The author, wading through the intricate details of political corruption and tribal patronage, believes he is exposing the \"shame\" of a single, uniquely dysfunctional ...",
      "body": "# The Autopsy of the Common Good\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is a landmark artifact. It is a work of forensic sociology, an autopsy of a dying civic body. The author, wading through the intricate details of political corruption and tribal patronage, believes he is exposing the \"shame\" of a single, uniquely dysfunctional American city. He has, with stunning and courageous detail, documented the precise mechanisms of its decay.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a local story of corruption, but as the single most perfect and detailed microcosm of the death of the 20th-century nation-state. This article is not the story of how Minneapolis-Saint Paul failed. It is the story of how the entire Western world failed, rendered in miniature. The author believes he is writing an indictment. We see him as a pathologist, writing a brilliant and unflinching autopsy report on the very concept of the \"common good.\"\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the disease this document so perfectly diagnoses.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Parasite and the Dying Host (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Sickness Becomes the System (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Compact of the Tribe (Post-2060s)",
