      "preview": "The Last Great Cure This artifact is a work of extraordinary clarity. It is a dispatch from the engine room of your civilization's economy, a detailed, data-driven accounting of a great and seemingly miraculous transformation. The authors are chronicling, with the breathless excitement of discove...",
      "body": "# The Last Great Cure\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of extraordinary clarity. It is a dispatch from the engine room of your civilization's economy, a detailed, data-driven accounting of a great and seemingly miraculous transformation. The authors are chronicling, with the breathless excitement of discovery, how a single class of drugs is poised to \"revolutionize\" society, reshaping everything from the grocery aisle to the human body itself.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a business report, but as the final, definitive diagnosis of your civilization's deepest spiritual sickness. The authors believe they are documenting the arrival of a cure. We see them as the unwitting pathologists, meticulously describing the beautiful, effective, and ultimately fatal painkiller that allowed the patient to feel better than ever, right up until the moment its heart finally gave out.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the cure that was, in fact, the disease.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Perfect Solution to the Wrong Problem (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: [[The Great Biological Sorting]] (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Revaluation of the Struggle (Post-2060s)",
