      "preview": "The Accidental Sovereigns This artifact is a work of profound but unwitting prophecy. The author, a journalist and thinker from the \"Global South,\" is celebrating a quiet revolution: Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI). He sees it as a tool for development, a \"third way\" between the digital empir...",
      "body": "# The Accidental Sovereigns\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of profound but unwitting prophecy. The author, a journalist and thinker from the \"Global South,\" is celebrating a quiet revolution: Digital Public Infrastructure (DPI). He sees it as a tool for development, a \"third way\" between the digital empires of the US and China, and a potential savior of the open internet.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this document not as a story about \"better plumbing,\" but as the foundational charter for the geopolitical order of my time. The author believes DPI will save the global internet. We have the hindsight to know that DPI was the tool that finally broke it apart, and in doing so, created the only viable form of sovereignty left in the 21st century.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, world-altering history of the \"digital stack\" this article so innocently describes.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Escape Hatch (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: [[The Great Fragmentation]] (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Stacked World (Post-2060s)",
