      "preview": "The Army of the Unloved This artifact is a work of sociological horror. The author, reviewing a documentary, has uncovered a ticking time bomb at the heart of the world's most populous nation. He sees a generation of \"surplus men,\" lonely, desperate, and increasingly resentful, being fed a diet o...",
      "body": "# The Army of the Unloved\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of sociological horror. The author, reviewing a documentary, has uncovered a ticking time bomb at the heart of the world's most populous nation. He sees a generation of \"surplus men,\" lonely, desperate, and increasingly resentful, being fed a diet of manipulative pickup artistry and state propaganda.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a film review, but as a strategic intelligence report on the formation of one of the most destabilizing forces of the 21st century. The author correctly identifies the link between sexual frustration and political violence. He sees the \"manosphere\" as a disjointed monster. We see it as the recruitment ground for the armies that would fight [[The Great Fragmentation]].\r\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of the \"surplus men\" this article describes.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: [[The Crisis of Posterity]] made Flesh (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Divergence of the Angry Young Man (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: [[The Engineered]] Solution (Post-2060s)",
