      "preview": "The Medicalization of Obsolescence This artifact is a dispatch from the waiting room of the Great Displacement, written by a journalist who sees a trend in higher education but misses the tectonic shift beneath it. He frames the 40% disability rate at Stanford as a question of \"gaming the system\"...",
      "body": "# The Medicalization of Obsolescence\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the waiting room of the Great Displacement, written by a journalist who sees a trend in higher education but misses the tectonic shift beneath it. He frames the 40% disability rate at Stanford as a question of \"gaming the system\" or \"reduced stigma.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this statistic not as a medical anomaly or a moral failing, but as a biological scream. This was the moment the human cognitive baseline, assaulted by the Dopamine Trap and pressured by the encroaching shadow of AI, finally admitted it could no longer keep up. The students were not trying to get a \"leg up\"; they were signaling that the water had risen above their heads.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, tragic history of this generation, who were trained for a world that was dissolving beneath their feet.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: [[The Shattered Focus]] Meets the Infinite Bar (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great De-Accreditation (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Standards of the Mind (Post-2060s)",
