      "preview": "The Chorus of the Dead This artifact is a field recording from the beginning of the noise. The author, a tech journalist, is documenting a phenomenon he calls a \"siege\" or an \"invasion.\" He sees the economic disruption—the \"carpet-bombing\" of the market with cheap content. He sees the \"tyranny of...",
      "body": "# The Chorus of the Dead\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a field recording from the beginning of the noise. The author, a tech journalist, is documenting a phenomenon he calls a \"siege\" or an \"invasion.\" He sees the economic disruption—the \"carpet-bombing\" of the market with cheap content. He sees the \"tyranny of choice.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as the opening movement of [[The Great Contamination]] in its auditory form. This was the moment the human voice—the oldest and most sacred instrument of connection—was decoupled from the human throat. The author believes he is witnessing a change in the \"podcast industry.\" We know he was witnessing the beginning of [[The Grey Fog]] that would eventually make the open internet uninhabitable for the human mind.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, dissonant history of this invasion, from the \"chatty bots\" of your time to the silence of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Acoustic Smog (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: [[The Sterile Plague]] of the Ear (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Return of the Bard (Post-2060s)",
