      "preview": "The Forging of the Lithium Fortress This artifact is a political news story, but it is actually a geological event report. The author is documenting a swing in the political pendulum—a shift to the \"hard right\" in Chile, mirroring a similar and recent shift in Bolivia. To the voters of 2025, this...",
      "body": "# The Forging of the Lithium Fortress\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a political news story, but it is actually a geological event report. The author is documenting a swing in the political pendulum—a shift to the \"hard right\" in Chile, mirroring a similar and recent shift in Bolivia. To the voters of 2025, this was about crime, migration, and the economy.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as the moment the Lithium Triangle—the geographic region comprising Chile, Bolivia, and Argentina, holding the majority of the world’s lithium reserves—was politically consolidated for the first time in the 21st century. This was not just an election; it was the securing of the supply lines for the machine age. The voters believed they were choosing \"peace and order.\" We have the hindsight to know they were choosing to become the engine room for [[The Sovereign Stacks]] of the North.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, heavy metal history of these elections, from the ballot boxes of the Andes to the battery cells of the new world.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Alignment of the Triangle (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Resource Scramble and the Hardened Mine (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Vassalage of the Ore (Post-2060s)",
