      "preview": "The Missing Cohort This is an artifact of profound sorrow and clear-eyed, personal historiography. The author, a man who \"almost\" had a career, is writing a memoir of professional failure. But it is not a story of individual inadequacy; it is a story of systemic displacement. He has meticulously ...",
      "body": "# The Missing Cohort\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis is an artifact of profound sorrow and clear-eyed, personal historiography. The author, a man who \"almost\" had a career, is writing a memoir of professional failure. But it is not a story of individual inadequacy; it is a story of systemic displacement. He has meticulously documented the \"invisible hand\" that pushed an entire demographic cohort—white male millennials—out of the institutions of culture, media, and academia.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a complaint about fairness, but as the origin story of [[The Invisible College]] and the Counter-Elite. The author is describing the creation of a surplus population of highly educated, culturally alienated, and economically precarious men. He wonders where they went. We know exactly where they went.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"lost generation,\" from the closed doors of Hollywood to the open frontiers of the new world.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Great Displacement (2014-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Forging of the Counter-Elite (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Patriarchs of the Stack (Post-2060s)",
