      "preview": "The Manifesto of the Plunder This artifact is a work of incandescent rage and strategic clarity. It is not an essay; it is a battle plan. The author, writing from the perspective of the \"virtual koryos,\" has correctly identified the moment of maximum leverage. He sees a generation of young men wh...",
      "body": "# The Manifesto of the Plunder\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of incandescent rage and strategic clarity. It is not an essay; it is a battle plan. The author, writing from the perspective of the \"virtual koryos,\" has correctly identified the moment of maximum leverage. He sees a generation of young men who have been economically and spiritually dispossessed, and he is offering them a path not to reconciliation, but to conquest.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as one of the most important foundational texts of [[The Great Culling]] and the Great De-Accreditation. It is the intellectual justification for the systemic looting and destruction of the 20th-century institutions. The author believes he is calling for justice. We see him lighting the fuse on the bomb that would blow the old world apart.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, violent history of this manifesto, from the angry blog posts of your time to the scorched earth of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Justification of the Wolf (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Kinetic Phase (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Aristocracy (Post-2060s)",
