      "preview": "The Last Audit of Empire This artifact is a work of geopolitical autopsy. The author, a strategic analyst, is reading the entrails of the National Security Strategy and the policies of the Trump administration, and correctly diagnosing them not as a plan for a new world order, but as the bankrupt...",
      "body": "# The Last Audit of Empire\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of geopolitical autopsy. The author, a strategic analyst, is reading the entrails of the National Security Strategy and the policies of the Trump administration, and correctly diagnosing them not as a plan for a new world order, but as the bankruptcy proceedings for the old one. He sees the \"business model\" of the empire shifting from hegemony to \"franchising,\" from free trade to a protectionist fortress.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as one of the most lucid early descriptions of the Great Shortening and the formation of the North American Sovereign Stack. The author believes he is analyzing a shift in US foreign policy. We know he is witnessing the geopolitical equivalent of a star collapsing into a black hole—the contraction of a global empire into a fortified regional singularity.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, kinetic history of this \"business model,\" from the tariffs of your time to the fortress walls of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Franchise Model (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Failure of Coercion (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Closed Loop (Post-2060s)",
