      "preview": "The Collapse of the Signal This artifact is a dispatch from the confusion of a collapsing market. The author is a journalist observing the breakdown of the entry-level hiring process. She sees a mess of grade inflation, AI-generated cover letters, and algorithmic filtering. She sees a \"weird Wild...",
      "body": "# The Collapse of the Signal\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the confusion of a collapsing market. The author is a journalist observing the breakdown of the entry-level hiring process. She sees a mess of grade inflation, AI-generated cover letters, and algorithmic filtering. She sees a \"weird Wild West\" where applicants and recruiters are locked in an arms race of synthetic noise.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a story about a bad job market, but as the definitive historical record of the moment the Signal-to-Noise Ratio of the 20th-century meritocracy dropped to zero. This was the end of the \"credential,\" the death of the \"resume,\" and the beginning of the brutal, necessary return to the only signal that cannot be faked: direct, physical proof of work.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, world-altering history of this breakdown, from the flooded inboxes of your time to the hard verification of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Great Noise (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Return of the Guild (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Reputation Economy (Post-2060s)",
