      "preview": "This artifact is a fever dream wrapped in a press release. It is a cheerful, corporate summary of a year that, from my perspective, was defined by the final, accelerating descent into cognitive and political chaos. The author, a blog writer for a massive platform, is celebrating \"pop culture.\" Sh...",
      "body": "This artifact is a fever dream wrapped in a press release. It is a cheerful, corporate summary of a year that, from my perspective, was defined by the final, accelerating descent into cognitive and political chaos. The author, a blog writer for a massive platform, is celebrating \"pop culture.\" She does not realize she is cataloging the symptoms of a terminal social pathology.\nThe most chilling detail is buried in the middle of the list. Charlie Kirk is listed as a \"Trending Topic\" and a \"Top Creator.\" Based on previous artifacts in our archive (specifically the Inception Point AI article and The Right Wing Coalition manifesto), we know that Kirk was assassinated earlier this year. The fact that he is still a \"Top Creator\" in December is the definitive proof of [[The Necromantic Internet]].\nAllow me to trace the full, uncanny history of this list, from the digital seance of your time to the silent archives of mine.\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Digital Seance (2020s-2030s)",
