      "body": "### A Eulogy for Guardrails\r\n\r\n\r\n### The Summary\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a remarkably clear-eyed diagnosis of a terminal social pathology. The author, Rob Henderson, correctly identifies the profound ideological and behavioral schism within the late-stage American empire: a credentialed elite that privately practiced the bourgeois virtues of discipline and family stability while publicly championing a \"nonjudgmental\" libertinism that proved corrosive to those outside their insulated class. Henderson believed he was witnessing a crisis of hypocrisy, a moral failing that could be corrected if the elite would simply \"preach what they practice.\" He was calling for a restoration of social guardrails by the very class that benefited from their selective removal.\r\n\r\nThrough the Hindsight Filter, we see this analysis not as a prescription, but as a field report from the final stages of Institutional Exhaustion. The phenomenon of \"luxury beliefs\" was not a simple hypocrisy; it was a structural feature of a social order that had become an abstract management system, completely decoupled from the lived reality of its peripheries. Henderson was documenting the moment when the managers of the system no longer believed in the public-facing operating system they enforced upon others. He thought he was observing a moral choice; we know he was recording the entropic and inevitable decay of a social contract that had already expired.\r### Act I: The Great Decoupling (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Consequence Cascade (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Reconstitution (Post-2060s)",
