      "preview": "The Architecture of Solipsism This artifact is a primary document from the final phase of Institutional Exhaustion. The authors, Sorota and Hendler, believed they were offering a constructive technical proposal to mend the fraying social contract of the American nation-state. They correctly ident...",
      "body": "### The Architecture of Solipsism\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a primary document from the final phase of Institutional Exhaustion. The authors, Sorota and Hendler, believed they were offering a constructive technical proposal to mend the fraying social contract of the American nation-state. They correctly identified the profound societal shift being forced by artificial intelligence—at the epistemic, agentic, and collective levels—but their proposed solutions were predicated on the fantasy that the 20th-century democratic institutions they sought to save still possessed the legitimacy and coherence to implement them.\r\n\r\nThrough the Hindsight Filter, we see this document not as a blueprint for salvation, but as an architectural drawing for the next phase of collapse. The authors thought they were designing buttresses to reinforce a weakened structure; in reality, they were cataloging the elegant new ways in which that structure would fly apart. Their call to build AI-mediated deliberative platforms was, in effect, a proposal to build a more efficient engine for the Great Fragmentation. They documented the symptoms of terminal polarization and prescribed the pathogen as the cure.\r### Act I: The Age of Augmented Solipsism (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Kinetic Deliberation (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Rise of Verifiable Polities (Post-2060s)",
