      "body": "# The Patient Zero of the Cyborg Age\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the frontier of cognitive evolution. The author, a journalist struggling with her own digital addiction, is not just writing a trend piece. She is documenting the precise moment when the human species split into two distinct cognitive phyla. She frames it as a choice between a \"smartphone\" and a \"dumbphone,\" but she intuits, correctly and terrifyingly, that it is a choice between two different definitions of the self.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for the Great Divergence. The author is Patient Zero of the Cyborg lineage. She admits, with a honesty that borders on horror, \"I am not addicted to my phone. I am my phone.\" This is the foundational creed of [[The Transcended]].\r\nAllow me to trace the full, branching history of this \"enmeshment,\" from the anxiety of your time to the speciation of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Cognitive Prosthetic (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Schism of the Mind (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Two Species (Post-2060s)",
