      "preview": "The Foreclosure of the Mind https://www.bloomberg.com/graphics/2026-college-enrollment-cliff/ This artifact is a dispatch from the edge of the demographic void. The authors, journalists for a financial publication, are documenting the \"cliff\" that American higher education is falling off of. They...",
      "body": "# The Foreclosure of the Mind\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://www.bloomberg.com/graphics/2026-college-enrollment-cliff/\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the edge of the demographic void. The authors, journalists for a financial publication, are documenting the \"cliff\" that American higher education is falling off of. They see a story of \"supply and demand,\" of a shrinking customer base and a \"painful rebalancing.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for the Great De-Accreditation. It is not a business story; it is the foreclosure notice for the 20th-century model of human capital formation. The colleges were not just businesses that ran out of customers; they were the organs of a body that had decided to stop growing.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"demographic drought,\" from the shuttered campuses of your time to [[The New Academies]] of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Collapse of the Mass Model (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Educational Sorting (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Academies (Post-2060s)",
