      "preview": "The Algorithm of the Tower of Babel This artifact is a eulogy for a shared world. The author, a media reporter for a business newspaper, is documenting the end of the \"monoculture.\" He sees a shift in business models, from broadcast to narrowcast. He sees a loss of shared experience. From my pers...",
      "body": "# The Algorithm of the Tower of Babel\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a eulogy for a shared world. The author, a media reporter for a business newspaper, is documenting the end of the \"monoculture.\" He sees a shift in business models, from broadcast to narrowcast. He sees a loss of shared experience.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for the Great Epistemic Divorce. The author is describing the precise mechanism by which the American population lost the ability to speak to itself. The death of the monoculture was not just a change in entertainment habits; it was the fragmentation of the collective unconscious. The \"unbridgeable gap\" he feels on the airplane was the fault line along which the nation would eventually split.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this fragmentation, from the niche streams of your time to the walled gardens of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Personalized Reality (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The War of the Narratives (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Curated Monoculture (Post-2060s)",
