      "preview": "The Temple of the Faustian Wild This artifact is a work of beautiful, romantic, and profoundly nostalgic ethnography. The author, writing in the winter of 2026, is exploring a retail store, but he sees a cathedral. He sees Bass Pro Shops not as a place to buy fishing rods, but as a \"folk-temple,\"...",
      "body": "# The Temple of the Faustian Wild\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of beautiful, romantic, and profoundly nostalgic ethnography. The author, writing in the winter of 2026, is exploring a retail store, but he sees a cathedral. He sees Bass Pro Shops not as a place to buy fishing rods, but as a \"folk-temple,\" a \"pedagogy for the deracinated,\" and a repository for the \"metaphysical undercurrent\" of the American soul.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for the Great Revaluation of the Real. The author is describing the precise emotional and spiritual hunger that would eventually drive the formation of the Bioconservative and Traditionalist Sovereign Stacks. He is documenting the moment when the \"bugman soul\" began to remember its body.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, wild history of this \"inland wilderness-basilica,\" from the retail therapy of your time to the survival mandate of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Simulation of Competence (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Costume Becomes the Uniform (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Sacred Grove of the Stack (Post-2060s)",
