      "body": "# The Swipe at the Silent Page\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a report from the nursery of a dying civilization. The author, a journalist for a major news outlet, is documenting a crisis of \"school readiness.\" She sees children who cannot dress themselves, cannot use a toilet, and who attempt to \"swipe\" the pages of a physical book as if it were a broken screen.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as an educational statistic, but as the clinical observation of a neurological mutiny. The human organism was rejecting the physical world. This was the moment when [[The Great Contamination]] crossed the blood-brain barrier of the next generation, rewiring their expectations of reality before they could even speak.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, devastating history of the \"swiping child,\" from the classrooms of your time to the Faraday cages of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Atrophy of the Real (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Unteachable Generation (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: [[The Analog Mandate]] (Post-2060s)",
