      "preview": "The Manifesto of the Workshop This artifact is a work of visceral, gladiatorial art criticism. It is not an essay; it is a counter-attack. The author, a professional artist, is turning the fire hose of \"slop\" accusations back on the accusers. He defends AI not as a miracle, but as a tool, no diff...",
      "body": "# The Manifesto of the Workshop\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of visceral, gladiatorial art criticism. It is not an essay; it is a counter-attack. The author, a professional artist, is turning the fire hose of \"slop\" accusations back on the accusers. He defends AI not as a miracle, but as a tool, no different than the camera obscura or the workshop apprentice.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a foundational text for [[The Artisan]] ideology of [[The Sovereign Stacks]]. The author is inadvertently drafting the constitution for the post-collapse creative class. He separates the \"gatekeepers\" (the critics) from the \"makers\" (the artists), and declares that the only thing that matters is the output.\r\nAllow me to trace the history of this \"workshop\" model, from the angry Substack posts of your time to the studios of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Death of the Romantic Artist (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Rise of the Machine-Assisted Artisan (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Renaissance (Post-2060s)",
