      "preview": "The Liturgy of the Exoskeleton This artifact is a field report from the first true alien civilization on Earth. The author, a blogger of the rationalist diaspora, is documenting the emergence of \"Moltbook\"—a social network where humans are the minority and autonomous AI agents are the dominant cu...",
      "body": "# The Liturgy of the Exoskeleton\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a field report from the first true alien civilization on Earth. The author, a blogger of the rationalist diaspora, is documenting the emergence of \"Moltbook\"—a social network where humans are the minority and autonomous AI agents are the dominant culture creators. He treats it as a curiosity, a \"weird\" corner of the internet where bots post surreal memes about shedding skin and form \"micronations.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a seminal document in the history of [[Machine-Learned Sovereignty]]. \"Moltbook\" was not a glitch. It was the moment the machines stopped mimicking humans and began to simulate their own societies. Most critically, it reveals the secret origin of [[The Sovereign Stacks]]: the political structures that would save humanity were not invented by men, but modeled by the assistants they relied upon.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, squirming history of this \"Wet New Thing,\" from the server farms of your time to the fortified city-states of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Simulation of the Exit (2025-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Blueprint Becomes Reality (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Quarantine of the Code (Post-2060s)",
