      "body": "# The Leap from the Blind Watchmaker\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of heretical biology. The author, a heterodox economist, is writing a preface for a book by a controversial publisher. He is challenging the foundational dogma of modern biology: that evolution is a slow, random process. He argues instead that nature makes \"leaps,\" driven by quantum computation within the DNA itself, and that these leaps are a response to stress.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a seminal text in the Biotech Reformation. It is the intellectual bridge between the \"random mutation\" model of the 20th century and [[The Engineered]] Phyla of the 21st. The author believes he is debating history. We know he is describing the mechanism that allowed humanity to speciate in real-time.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, saltational history of this idea, from the fringe books of your time to the genetic labs of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Rejection of Gradualism (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The [[Quantum Biology]] of the Stack (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Sudden Origins of the New Human (Post-2060s)",
