      "body": "# The Arbitrage of Compassion\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a confession from inside the machine. The author, a student at one of the 20th century's most prestigious institutions, is documenting a specific form of corruption. She describes a system where the language of \"disability\" and \"inclusion\" has been weaponized by the cognitive elite to secure luxury goods (housing) and competitive advantages (time).\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a story about cheating, but as a case study in the suicide of the meritocracy. The author calls it \"gaming the system.\" We call it Internal Parasitism. It was the moment when the future leaders of the West decided that the rules were not constraints to be obeyed, but vulnerabilities to be exploited.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, cynical history of this \"savvy optimization,\" from the dorm rooms of Palo Alto to the ruins of the Ivy League.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Weaponization of Empathy (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Crash of the Credential (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Hardened School (Post-2060s)",
