      "body": "# The First Flash of the Perimeter\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the confusion of a borderland. The journalists are reporting on a \"chaotic\" airspace closure caused by a mix of cartel drones, military lasers, and a stray party balloon. They frame it as a bureaucratic failure and a public relations disaster.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as the first live-fire drill of [[The Architecture of Pervasive Security]]. It was the moment the United States admitted that it had lost the monopoly on the low skies. The \"Department of War\" (a telling rebranding noted in the text) was not just testing a laser; it was testing the immune system of the future fortress.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, blinding history of this skirmish, from the panic in El Paso to the silent, laser-guarded skies of my time.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Asymmetry of the Swarm (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Closing of the Sky (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Iron Sky (Post-2060s)",
