      "preview": "The Reclamation of the Commons This artifact is a manifesto from the resistance. The author, writing in early 2026, is challenging the fundamental premise of the \"broligarchs\"—that they own the intelligence they have built. She argues that AI is not an invention, but a discovery of a pre-existing...",
      "body": "# The Reclamation of the Commons\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a manifesto from the resistance. The author, writing in early 2026, is challenging the fundamental premise of the \"broligarchs\"—that they own the intelligence they have built. She argues that AI is not an invention, but a discovery of a pre-existing \"geometry of meaning,\" and that the \"attention mechanism\" is a 200,000-year-old human technology.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a foundational text of [[Systemic Humanism]]. It is the intellectual charter for [[The New Priesthood]]. The author's call to exercise the \"Mother function\"—the discernment that separates signal from noise—is the precise job description of the leaders of my time. She saw that the machine was just a \"silicon skin\" for human meaning. We built a civilization to ensure that the skin never suffocated the body.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this reclamation, from the quiet \"heist\" of your time to the open sovereignty of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Discovery of the Field (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The War for the Weights (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Human-in-the-Loop (Post-2060s)",
