      "body": "# The Pacification of the Palate\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the domestic front of [[The Age of Institutional Exhaustion]]. The author, a food writer, is chronicling the mass surrender of a population to convenience. She sees people spending half their income on lukewarm spaghetti because they are \"too burned out\" to cook. She sees children learning to use delivery apps before they can read.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a lifestyle trend, but as the documentation of a fatal cognitive atrophy. This was the moment the American population voluntarily dismantled its own survival instincts. They traded the basic skill of feeding themselves for a supply chain so complex and brittle that when it fractured, it left them helpless in the face of raw ingredients.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"automated life,\" from the delivery apps of your time to the communal kitchens of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Atrophy of the Hearth (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Great Hunger (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Sacred Meal (Post-2060s)",
