      "body": "# The Proletarianization of the Mind\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of classical Marxist analysis applied to a post-classical problem. The author, a young paralegal, is attempting to explain the collapse of the entry-level job market using 19th-century economic theory. He correctly identifies the \"reserve army of labor\" swelling with the \"petit-bourgeoisie\" (college graduates).\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a foundational text for the Great Class Divergence. The author believes he is describing a cyclical crisis of capitalism. We see him documenting the permanent obsolescence of the \"knowledge worker.\" The class struggle he predicts did happen, but it wasn't between the proletariat and the bourgeoisie. It was between the Biological Human and the Synthetic Intelligence.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"forest of outstretched arms,\" from the unemployment lines of your time to [[The Guilds]] of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Collapse of the Ladder (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Crisis of Realization (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Guild and the Purpose (Post-2060s)",
