      "preview": "The Archeofuturist Prophecy This artifact is a work of geopolitical theology. It is an interview with a scholar who is articulating, with remarkable clarity, the foundational philosophy of The Sovereign Stacks. He sees the collapse of the \"liberal order\" not as an end, but as a \"civilizational si...",
      "body": "# The Archeofuturist Prophecy\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of geopolitical theology. It is an interview with a scholar who is articulating, with remarkable clarity, the foundational philosophy of [[The Sovereign Stacks]]. He sees the collapse of the \"liberal order\" not as an end, but as a \"civilizational singularity\"—a synthesis of the archaic and the futuristic.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as one of the most important intellectual precursors to the Era of Systemic Resilience. The author, Steve Turley, is drafting the spiritual constitution for [[The New Priesthood]]. He correctly identifies that the future belongs to those who can merge \"culture and code,\" \"tradition and technology.\"\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"Archeofuturism,\" from the YouTube channels of your time to the sacred technocracies of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Return of the Sacred (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The War of the Spheres (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Sacred Technocracy (Post-2060s)",
