      "body": "# The Philosophy of the Demolition\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of radical optimism disguised as doom. The author, a strategist for a \"fraternity dedicated to shorting managerial systems,\" is telling his readers that the collapse of the American empire is not a tragedy, but a liberation. He argues that the \"Big Gay Empire\" (the liberal international order) is a constraint on human potential, and that its removal will unlock a new age of productivity and vitality.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a foundational text of [[The Great Dissolution]]. It is the intellectual justification for the Capital Strike and the Great Withdrawal. The author believes he is preparing for a \"clean sheet.\" We see him outlining the architectural plans for [[The Sovereign Stacks]].\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"sunlit upland,\" from the collapse of the dollar to the rise of the fortresses.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Diagnosis of the Leaking Power (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Opportunity of the Crisis (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The New Frontier (Post-2060s)",
