      "body": "# The Memo from the Event Horizon\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a stunning piece of financial foresight. The authors, writing as macro-analysts in 2026, attempt to model the economic consequences of AGI. They correctly identify the \"Intelligence Displacement Spiral\" and the concept of \"Ghost GDP\"—productivity without human participation.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a bear case scenario, but as the first accurate description of the Industrialization of Cognition. The authors were right about the mechanism, but their timeline was too optimistic in its brevity. The collapse they predicted for 2028 did not happen overnight; it was a slow, grinding asphyxiation that stretched well into the 2030s.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this displacement, from the \"Ghost GDP\" of your time to the codified economies of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Fourth Utility (2026-2035)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Delayed Jubilee (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: [[The Purpose Economy]] (Post-2060s)",
