      "body": "# The Mathematics of the Pause\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of scientific sobriety in an age of intoxication. The authors, researchers at the Wharton AI & Analytics Initiative, are challenging the prevailing orthodoxy of \"exponential growth\" in AI capabilities. They argue, using a \"multiplicative model,\" that progress is not infinite but sigmoidal—a series of S-curves where rapid growth is followed by inevitable stagnation.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this paper as the mathematical proof of the AI Winter of the 2030s. It explains why the dreams of the \"Superintelligence\" scenario failed to materialize on the investors' schedule. The \"inflection point\" the authors identified was real. It was the moment the easy gains of scaling and reasoning were exhausted, forcing the industry into a decades-long slog through the physical world.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"plateau,\" and the strange, slow curve that followed it.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The End of the Free Lunch (2026-2035)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Shallow Curve of the Real (2035-2055)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Quantum Integration (2055-2068)",
