      "body": "# The Schism of the Stroller\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://archive.is/TGjta\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the domestic front of [[The Great Dissolution]]. The author, a journalist and mother, is chronicling the breakup of a neighborhood parenting group. She sees a story about \"boundaries\" and \"political polarization.\" She frames it as a local conflict exacerbated by national tensions.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for [[The Great Physical Sorting]]. The \"schism\" described here was not an argument; it was the cellular division of the American body politic. The parents of Petworth were not just disagreeing; they were sorting themselves into the embryonic forms of two distinct and incompatible civilizations.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, divergent history of these two groups, from the WhatsApp chats of your time to the separate realities of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Incompatibility of the Commons (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Formalization of the Tribe (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Divergent Curricula (Post-2060s)",
