      "body": "# The Casino of the Collapse\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of terrifying financial foresight. The author, a crypto-analyst writing in early 2026, is documenting the convergence of open-source intelligence and decentralized finance. He sees \"permissionless prediction markets\" turning war into a tradable asset. He worries about \"reflexivity\"—the idea that betting on an event might cause the event to happen.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a theory, but as the founding charter of the War Economy that fueled [[The Great Fragmentation]]. The author asks, \"Who benefits from acceleration?\" The answer was: everyone who held a short position on civilization. This was the moment when the collapse ceased to be a tragedy and became a profitable trade.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, bloody history of this \"gamification of geopolitics,\" from the dashboards of 2026 to the closed markets of the Stacks.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Assassination Markets (2026-2035)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Liquidity of Chaos (2035-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The De-Financialization of War (Post-2060s)",
