      "body": "# The Automation of Intimacy\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the final, confused years of the 20th-century dating market. The author, a journalist struggling with her own romantic life, is documenting the integration of AI into the courtship process. She sees apps that rewrite bios, generate flirtatious messages, and use biometrics to \"quantify desire.\" She also notes a nascent backlash—a return to \"IRL\" events and matchmakers.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this as a primary source document for [[The Great Unpairing]]. The author believes she is witnessing a \"fix\" for a broken system. We see the final, fatal automation of the human heart, a process that rendered genuine connection so efficient it became meaningless, accelerating the demographic collapse of the West.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"optimized love,\" from the swipe fatigue of your time to the arranged marriages of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: [[The Sterile Plague]] of the Heart (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Bifurcation of Mating (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Arranged Future (Post-2060s)",
