      "body": "# The Doctrine of the Harpoon\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a work of cold, kinetic strategy disguised as environmental protection. The author, writing for a defense think tank in early 2026, is proposing a radical escalation: using military force to sink fishing boats. He calls it \"Kinetic Conservation.\"\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a proposal, but as the founding charter of the [[Resource Fortress]] strategy that would define [[The Supply Chain Wars]]. The author believes he is saving fish. We know he is outlining the rules of engagement for the first great maritime conflict of the 21st century.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, bloody history of this \"Blue Shield,\" from the policy paper of your time to the automated kill zones of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The End of the High Seas (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Kinetic Phase (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Closed Ocean (Post-2060s)",
