      "body": "# The Enclosure of the Eye\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the front lines of [[The Great Contamination]]. The author, a journalist for a tech-skeptic outlet, is documenting the degradation of a beloved platform into \"AI slop\" and automated censorship. He interviews artists who are fighting a losing battle against algorithms that steal their work, mislabel it, and then ban them for trying to fix it.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a story about bad customer service, but as a primary source document for the Death of the Public Archive. Pinterest was one of the last repositories of human visual culture. Its corruption was a key event in [[The Grey Fog]]—the moment when the digital memory of the 20th century became unreliable, forcing the survivors to abandon the cloud and return to physical libraries.\r\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"enclosure,\" from the frustrated artists of your time to the curated vaults of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Poisoning of the Well (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Flight to the Physical (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Curated Vault (Post-2060s)",
