      "body": "# The Ouroboros of the Mind\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the final, absurd days of the 20th-century university. The author describes a professor attempting to save the integrity of education by using AI to grade students who are using AI to cheat. It is a perfect, closed loop: machines generating text, machines evaluating text, with the human mind reduced to a mere conduit for the data.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as an educational innovation, but as the final capitulation of the Great De-Accreditation. The professor believed he was \"fighting fire with fire.\" In reality, he was burning down the school to save the grading curve. He demonstrated that the institution no longer had the human capacity to validate its own existence.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, circular history of this \"automated inquisition,\" from the classrooms of NYU to the tribunals of the Stacks.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Collapse of the Artifact (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Era of [[The Continuous Audit]] (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Human Tribunal (Post-2060s)",
