      "body": "# The Promethean Pet\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis artifact is a story of incredible determination and technological triumph. The author, a journalist for a major Australian newspaper, is chronicling the heartwarming tale of a tech entrepreneur who used AI to cure his dying dog. She frames it as a victory for \"citizen science\" and a hopeful sign for the future of human medicine.\r\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this document not as a pet rescue story, but as the moment the seal broke on Democratized Bioweaponry. The author believes she is writing about a cure. We see her documenting the exact methodology that allowed an amateur, armed with a chatbot and a credit card, to design a novel, custom-built biological agent in his living room.\r\nAllow me to trace the full, terrifying history of this \"magical\" breakthrough, from the veterinary clinics of your time to the quarantine zones of mine.\r\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\r### Act I: The Democratization of the Code (2020s-2030s)\r\r\r\r### Act II: The Era of the Garage Plague (2030s-2050s)\r\r\r\r### Act III: The Purity of the Fortress (Post-2060s)",
