      "body": "### **The Weight of the Wind**\n\n\nThis artifact is a work of thermodynamic accounting. The author, writing for a climate-skeptic European institute in early 2026, is performing a brutal mathematical audit on the German energy transition (*Energiewende*). He calculates the sheer, staggering mass of batteries required to back up an intermittent renewable grid: \"60 million tons of battery for ten days of electricity.\"\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a political argument, but as the precise mathematical definition of the **AI Energy Wall** hitting the European continent. The author believes he is critiquing Green policy. We see him documenting the exact physical limits that would soon force the **Triage Economy** and the balkanization of the European grid.\n\nAllow me to trace the full, heavy history of this \"Deutschland-Batterie,\" from the spreadsheets of your time to the hardened reactors of mine.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Delusion of Infinite Storage (2020s-2030s)",
