      "body": "### **The Hallmarking of the Soul**\n\n\nThis artifact is a dispatch from the frantic, early days of the **Revaluation of the Real**. The author, a journalist for a legacy broadcaster, is observing a chaotic marketplace trying to invent a new standard of value. They see a \"backlash\" against automation and a confused scramble for \"AI-free\" logos, comparing it to the \"Fair Trade\" movement.\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a consumer protection story, but as the birth of the **Artisan Class** and the first crude attempts to quantify the **Convivial Mandate**. The people in this article are not just trying to sell books or movies; they are trying to establish the economic and spiritual boundary between the human and the machine. They are inventing the hallmark for the soul.\n\nAllow me to trace the full, rigorous history of this \"certification,\" from the confusing stamps of your time to the immutable ledgers of mine.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Panic of the Counterfeit (2020s-2030s)",
