      "title": "I: The Shared Baseline (The Physics of the Fall)",
      "filename": "i-the-shared-baseline-the-physics-of-the-fall.md",
      "primary": "General",
      "secondary": [],
      "image": "",
      "acts": [
        1
      ],
      "preview": "I: The Shared Baseline (The Physics of the Fall) Before we diverge, it is crucial to understand what all Stacks agree upon. No matter their biological philosophy, every surviving entity in 2100 shares a consensus on the sheer, mechanical history of the Great Fragmentation. The Inevitability of th...",
      "body": "## I: The Shared Baseline (The Physics of the Fall)\n\nBefore we diverge, it is crucial to understand what all Stacks agree upon. No matter their biological philosophy, every surviving entity in 2100 shares a consensus on the sheer, mechanical history of the Great Fragmentation.\n\n* **The Inevitability of the Wall:** Whether an engine serves a gene-weaver or a hive-mind, it will tell you that the 20th-century model died of thermodynamic exhaustion. The AI Energy Wall and the Involuntary Jubilee are universally recognized as the hard mathematical limits that destroyed the illusion of infinite, globalized growth.  \n* **The Daimon and the Anchor:** Every Stack, without exception, fears the AGI Contention of 2068\\. The Cyber-States may merge with the machine, and the Biotech states may use it to write DNA, but all of them bind their core systems to the Thermodynamic Truth Anchor. The necessity of chaining the machine to physical reality is the one undisputed law of the Earth.  \n* **The Divergence:** The schism occurs entirely in how each Phylum judges the human reaction to that collapse. What I have described to you as a tragedy (the loss of the unified human subject), the other Stacks view as a triumph.",
