      "body": "### **The Replacement of the Last Bridge**\n\n\nThis artifact is a document of profound, structural geopolitical divorce. The author, writing in early 2026, is chronicling the massive, expensive, and desperate effort by the European Union to untangle its nervous system from that of the United States and its corporate proxies. He frames this as an awakening, a continent finally willing to pay the \"price tag\" of sovereignty to avoid the whims of American billionaires and politicians.\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a story of European triumph, but as the logistical blueprint for the Great Fragmentation. The author believes he is describing the European Union securing its place in a multilateral world. We know he is describing the exact mechanics of how a globalized planet snapped into the isolated, autarkic Sovereign Stacks of my time.\n\nAllow me to trace the full, expensive history of this \"breakup letter,\" from the satellite constellations of your time to the hardened firewalls of mine.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Parasovereign Veto (2020s-2030s)",
