      "preview": "The Theology of the Spreadsheet This artifact is a fascinating hybrid of corporate management theory and Biblical exegesis. The author, a venture capitalist of the 2020s \"Right Wing\" coalition, is attempting to construct a theological justification for executive power in the age of AI. He equates...",
      "body": "### **The Theology of the Spreadsheet**\n\n\nThis artifact is a fascinating hybrid of corporate management theory and Biblical exegesis. The author, a venture capitalist of the 2020s \"Right Wing\" coalition, is attempting to construct a theological justification for executive power in the age of AI. He equates the structuring of corporate data (creating an \"ontology\") with Adam’s divine mandate to name the animals in Genesis. He warns that outsourcing this task to AI or progressive bureaucracy is a sinful abdication of human dominion.\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this document not as a business strategy, but as the foundational theology of the *Builder Stacks*. The author is wrestling with the exact existential terror of his era—the realization that humanity was surrendering its sovereignty to autonomous systems. His proposed solution—a fierce, unapologetic, and religiously justified assertion of human control over the digital architecture—became the governing philosophy of the factions that survived the Great Fragmentation.\n\nAllow me to trace the full history of this \"dominion mandate,\" from the boardrooms of your time to the command centers of mine.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Rebellion Against the Managerial Swarm (2020s-2030s)",
