      "body": "### **The Metrics of the Autocannibal**\n\n\nThis artifact is a work of exceptional, agonizing diagnostic clarity. The author, writing just before the structural collapse of the late 2020s, uses the historical bankruptcies of retail giants to explain the suicidal logic of the AI-driven layoffs occurring in his own time. He correctly identifies that organizations do not die from technological disruption; they die from a self-inflicted blindness induced by the worship of short-term metrics.\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a business school case study, but as the precise description of the mechanism that triggered the Great De-Accreditation and the Involuntary Jubilee. The author calls it \"losing their minds.\" We call it Autocannibalism. The corporate entities of your era were stripping the copper wiring out of their own walls to meet the quarterly energy bill, all while celebrating the \"efficiency\" of the darkness that followed.\n\nAllow me to trace the full history of this disease, from the spreadsheets of 2026 to the hardened, physical ledgers of my time.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Hallucination of the Spreadsheet (2020s-2030s)",
