      "body": "### **The Seance of the Civic Ghost**\n\n\nThis artifact is a document of profound and localized grief. The author, analyzing the decay of leadership in a Midwestern American city, is tracing the ghost of a civic structure that had already evaporated. He uses an early Large Language Model to prove what he already intuitively knows: the people who run the city no longer own the city, and the people who own the city no longer care about it.\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a complaint about municipal politics, but as a forensic tracking of the Parasovereign migration. The author believes he is writing about the loss of \"movers and shakers.\" We see him describing the exact sociological mechanism that created the Feral Cities and paved the way for the Sovereign Stacks.\n\nAllow me to trace the full, structural history of this \"leadership deficit,\" from the hollowed-out boardrooms of your time to the fortified walls of mine.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Extraction of the Apex (1980s-2020s)",
