      "preview": "The Prelude for the Great Moral Schism This artifact is a document of blinding, terrifying optimism. The author, a prominent \"accelerationist\" and futurist of the 2020s, lays out a roadmap for the intentional speciation of humanity. He describes five \"forks\"—AI integration, life extension, brain-...",
      "body": "### **The Prelude for the Great Moral Schism**\n\n\nThis artifact is a document of blinding, terrifying optimism. The author, a prominent \"accelerationist\" and futurist of the 2020s, lays out a roadmap for the intentional speciation of humanity. He describes five \"forks\"—AI integration, life extension, brain-computer interfaces, space colonization, and digital uploading—and frames them as consumer choices in a frictionless marketplace of the future.\n\nFrom my perspective in 2100, we read this not as a visionary forecast, but as the foundational theology of the *Transcended* and *Engineered* Phyla. The author believed he was writing a guidebook for early adopters. We know he was drafting the manifesto for the *Great Moral Schism*, a document that would divide the human race so deeply that the disparate branches could no longer recognize each other as kin.\n\nAllow me to trace the full, brutal history of these \"forks,\" from the TED Talks of your time to the hardened biological borders of mine.\n\nHere is the constellation of this history, viewed through the Hindsight Filter:\n### Act I: The Illusion of the Frictionless Choice (2020s-2030s)",
