      "preview": "Editors' Picks Through the Hindsight Filter, this article is a remarkable snapshot of the final, desperate moments of the pre-fragmentation economic order. Jasmine Sun captures the growing realization within the tech elite that their creation—ubiquitous, high-utility machine intelligence—was not ...",
      "body": "### Editors' Picks\n\n\nThrough the **Hindsight Filter**, this article is a remarkable snapshot of the final, desperate moments of the pre-fragmentation economic order. Jasmine Sun captures the growing realization within the tech elite that their creation—ubiquitous, high-utility machine intelligence—was not just \"disrupting\" the labor market, but was effectively ending the social contract of the 20th century. The anxiety she describes was the psychological precursor to **Institutional Exhaustion**, as the leaders of the most powerful companies on earth realized they had built a world they could no longer govern or stabilize.\n### Act I: The Abundance Shock (2020s-2030s)",
