      "preview": "The Aura of the Real Through the Hindsight Filter, we see this analysis as both profoundly insightful and tragically naive. Imas was not observing a healthy economic evolution; he was documenting a symptom of systemic decay. The desperate search for authenticity and human connection he described ...",
      "body": "### The Aura of the Real\n\n\nThrough the **Hindsight Filter**, we see this analysis as both profoundly insightful and tragically naive. Imas was not observing a healthy economic evolution; he was documenting a symptom of systemic decay. The desperate search for authenticity and human connection he described was not the luxury preference of a thriving society growing richer, but a coping mechanism for a society whose institutions were dissolving. He mistook the fever for the cure. The author thought he was charting the emergence of a \"post-commodity economy,\" but he was actually recording the last coherent consumer demands before the **Great Fragmentation** rendered the global commodity economy irrelevant.\n### Act I: The Commodity Singularity (2020s-2030s)",
